<p>NOTE: During the second quarter of 1996, the company redeemed its nine percent Sinking Fund Debentures resulting in an extraordinary net loss on early extinguishment of debt of $2 million and reduced net income applicable to common stock by a $52.1 million premium on the redemption of the company's preference stock.</p>
<p>During the first quarter of 1996, the company recorded a tax benefit of $104.5 million on the portion of a special cash dividend paid to the Manville Personal Injury Settlement Trust. In addition, the company recorded a net gain of $177.2 million on the disposition of its 81.3 percent interest in Riverwood International Corporation and recorded an extraordinary net loss of $314.3 million on the settlement of the Trust's profit sharing right to 20 percent of the Company's adjusted net earnings.</p>
